cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, the census method or the blindspot tool, please cite it as below."
title: "advisory-import-census: a reproducible census of maintainer-published GitHub security advisories that never reach the global Advisory Database for self-hosted AI/ML tools"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, public-data census measuring the "advisory-import gap":
  security advisories that maintainers publish as GitHub repository security
  advisories (GRAs) but that never reach the global GitHub Advisory Database
  under their own GHSA ID, leaving them invisible to Dependabot, npm audit,
  pip-audit and OSV. The 2026-10-14 snapshot surveys 30 widely used self-hosted
  AI/ML projects: of 618 published advisories, 195 (31.6%) are not present in the
  global database under their own GHSA ID, with a median of 91.1 days missing.
  Version 0.2.0 adds blindspot.py, a standard-library tool that runs the same
  check on any project's own dependencies; version 0.3.0 packages it as a
  composite GitHub Action that gates CI and writes a job-summary report; version
  0.4.0 adds pyproject.toml support (PEP 621 and Poetry) to both the tool and the
  Action, and ships blindspot as the console command advisory-blindspot.
